{
  "version": 4,
  "_note": "Vocabulary for classifying employer replies (code/mailbox.py --replies). Person-independent, like sources/professions.json: the phrases are a property of the language, not of the job seeker. Swiss employers write EN/DE/FR, so all three are covered. Keys of `kinds` are tried in file order and the first keyword that appears in subject+body wins - offer before rejection before interview before ack, because a rejection mail often says 'thank you for the interview'. Matching is plain lowercase substring, so German umlauts and accents must be written as they appear; a typographic apostrophe is folded to a plain one first, so write won't, not won’t. No bare 'interview' and no 'next step': acknowledgements say both ('if there is a fit we will be in touch about next steps'), and with interview ahead of ack every Ashby receipt read as an interview (2026-09-24). An interview phrase has to be the invitation itself.",
